        .beekeeperLogWelcomeBackFmt: "While you were away, the bees made %@ honey.",
        .beekeeperLogWelcomeBackNothing: "The bees are glad you're back.",
        .helpBeekeeperObjective: "Catch bees and look after a hive. The bees make honey on their own, the honey turns into wax, and a friendly bear trades Beebits for your honey. There is no score and no end: the hive simply grows at its own pace.",
        .helpBeekeeperHowToPlay: "1. Catch Bee: each click adds bees to your hive. With bare hands, a bee sometimes stings you and gets away.\n2. Honey: every bee makes a little honey each second. When the combs are full, the extra honey doesn't fit, but it still counts towards wax.\n3. Wax: every 50 honey the bees make gives 1 wax, even when the combs are full.\n4. The Bear: once you hold 10 honey, a bear comes by. Trade 10 honey for 1 Beebit, or Trade all.\n5. The Shop: spend Beebits on better tools (each catches more bees, and none of them sting) and on the Wax-Catcher (twice the wax). Tools are bought in order.\n6. Combs: spend wax to build a comb. Each comb holds 200 more honey, and each new comb costs a little more wax.",
        .helpBeekeeperAwayTitle: "🌙 While You're Away",
        .helpBeekeeperAway: "The hive keeps working while you play another game, and even while Honeycomb is closed, for up to 3 days. When the combs are full, no more honey is stored until you make room, but wax keeps coming. Your hive is saved automatically. New Game starts a brand-new hive, and asks first if you have bees to lose.",
