        .beekeeperLogWaspRaidGuardsFmt: "The wasp helps itself to %@ honey. The guards keep every bee safe.",
        .beekeeperLogShoeMissGuardsFmt: "Missed. The wasp helps itself to %@ honey. The guards keep every bee safe.",
        .helpBeekeeperGardenTitle: "🌱 The Garden",
        .helpBeekeeperGarden: "The Hippies and the wasps sometimes give you a seed, and you can see what kind it is. Plant it in a free bed (you have two beds, so two seeds can grow at once; the Shop sells a third) and wait: each plant takes its own time to sprout, even while the app is closed, and gives your hive a specialty.\n\nWildflowers and clover give foraging: a steady 3 pollen a minute each. Pollen and honey make bee bread at The Workbench, and bee bread plus wax pays for moving your bees into a wooden hive, where every honeybee makes more honey. A bramble gives guarding: every honeybee makes 25% more honey. The willow (about an hour) gives nursing: the queen lays 50% faster, and eats bee bread faster too. The poplar (about 6 hours, a seed from the wasps once you trade with them) gives resin: the bees gather propolis, which goes into candles and the Propolis Seal. Clover takes about 12 hours.\n\nPaper from the wasps buys the Beekeeper's Notebook, with a note about each thing your hive can do, and a Third Bed.",
